    "prompt": "A bus starts with some children. At the first stop, 5 children get off and 7 get on. At the second stop, half of the children on the bus get off, then 4 get on. There are now 13 children on the bus. How many children were on the bus at the start?",
    "options": [],
    "visuals": [],
    "answerKey": {
      "kind": "number",
      "value": 16,
      "tolerance": 0
    },
    "explanation": "Work backwards. Before the last 4 joined, 13 - 4 = 9 children remained. This was half the bus, so there were 18 before that stop. Undo the first stop: 18 - 7 + 5 = 16 children at the start. Check: 16 - 5 + 7 = 18; half remain, then 4 join, giving 13.",
